-- title:
--   No cyclotomic p-torsion point with unipotent special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and fix a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal generated by $p$ in $\mathbb{Z}_p$ (so that it is the reduction map). Let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ which is finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module and whose comultiplication is cocommutative, and assume that the Cartier dual of the base change $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$, that is the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual `Module.Dual` of $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ with its convolution ring structure, is a local ring. Let $f$ be an element of the group `WithConv` of $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ under convolution with $f^p = 1$, and suppose: for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p)$ lying in the image, under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup, of the inertia subgroup of the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$, for every $c \in \mathbb{N}$ with $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^c$ for all $\zeta$ satisfying $\zeta^p = 1$, and for every $g$ in that convolution group with $g(h) = \sigma(f(h))$ for all $h \in H$, one has $g = f^c$. Then $f = 1$.
--
--   In scheme language: a finite flat group scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ ($p$ odd) whose special fibre has unipotent Cartier dual admits no non-trivial $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$-point of order dividing $p$ on which inertia acts through the mod $p$ cyclotomic character; this is the local, $\mathbb{Z}_p$-coefficient form of a result of Raynaud used in the analysis of finite flat models. It is cited in the construction of unipotent models for locally flat cocycles in [`ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_model_of_isLocallyFlatCocycleAd_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.exists_unipotent_model_of_isLocallyFlatCocycleAd_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual).
